), which corresponds to a \\(90^\\circ\\) counterclockwise rotation.\n\nThe multiplication of a complex number \\(a + bi\\) by \\(i\\) is given by:\n\\[i \\cdot (a + bi) = i \\cdot a + i \\cdot bi = ai + bi^2 = ai - b = -b + ai\\]\n\nSo, for the complex number \\(7 + 2i\\), the resulting complex number after a \\(90^\\circ\\) counterclockwise rotation is:\n\\[i \\cdot (7 + 2i) = -2 + 7i\\]\n\nLet's confirm this using Python code.\n```python\n# Define the complex number\nz = 7 + 2j\n\n# Rotate the complex number by 90 degrees counterclockwise (multiply by i)\nrotated_z = z * 1j\n\n# Output the resulting complex number\nprint(rotated_z)\n```\n```output\n(-2+7j)\n```\nThe resulting complex number after rotating \\(7 + 2i\\) by \\(90^\\circ\\) counterclockwise around the origin is \\(\\boxed{-2 + 7i}\\).", "To find the result of a $90^\\circ$ counter-clockwise rotation of the complex number $7 + 2i$ around the origin, we can use the fact that a $90^\\circ$ counter-clockwise rotation of a complex number $z = a + bi$ is equivalent to multiplying $z$ by $i$. \n\nSo, the new complex number after the rotation will be:\n\\[ (7 + 2i) \\cdot i = 7i + 2i^2 = 7i + 2(-1) = -2 + 7i. \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the complex number\nz = 7 + 2j\n\n# Perform the 90 degree counter-clockwise rotation\nrotated_z = z * 1j\n\n# Print the resulting complex number\nprint(rotated_z)\n```\n```output\n(-2+7j)\n```\nThe resulting complex number after a $90^\\circ$ counter-clockwise rotation of $7 + 2i$ is $\\boxed{-2 + 7i}$.", "To determine the result of a $90^\\circ$ counter-clockwise rotation around the origin for the complex number $7 + 2i$, we can use the property of complex numbers that a $90^\\circ$ counter-clockwise rotation corresponds to multiplication by $i$.\n\nSo, we need to compute $(7 + 2i) \\cdot i$.\n\nLet's perform the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n(7 + 2i) \\cdot i = 7i + 2i^2\n\\]\n\nSince $i^2 = -1$, we can substitute this in:\n\n\\[\n7i + 2(-1) =