ulfill a person's daily caloric requirement, we can set up a simple equation based on the information given. If $40$ calories is $2\\%$ of a person's daily caloric requirement, we can express this as:\n\n\\[ 40 = 0.02 \\times \\text{Total Daily Caloric Requirement} \\]\n\nTo find the total daily caloric requirement, we can rearrange the equation to solve for the Total Daily Caloric Requirement:\n\n\\[ \\text{Total Daily Caloric Requirement} = \\frac{40}{0.02} \\]\n\nNow let's calculate this using Python.\n```python\n# Given values\ncalories_snack = 40\npercentage_of_daily_requirement = 0.02\n\n# Calculate total daily caloric requirement\ntotal_daily_caloric_requirement = calories_snack / percentage_of_daily_requirement\nprint(total_daily_caloric_requirement)\n```\n```output\n2000.0\n```\nThe total number of calories that fulfill a person's daily caloric requirement is \\(\\boxed{2000}\\).", "To determine the total daily caloric requirement, we can set up a simple equation based on the information given. If $40$ calories is $2\\%$ of the daily caloric requirement, we can express this as:\n\n\\[ 40 = 0.02 \\times \\text{Total Daily Caloric Requirement} \\]\n\nTo find the total daily caloric requirement, we can rearrange the equation to solve for the total:\n\n\\[ \\text{Total Daily Caloric Requirement} = \\frac{40}{0.02} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values\ncalories_in_tin = 40\npercentage_of_daily_requirement = 0.02\n\n# Calculate total daily caloric requirement\ntotal_daily_caloric_requirement = calories_in_tin / percentage_of_daily_requirement\nprint(total_daily_caloric_requirement)\n```\n```output\n2000.0\n```\nThe total daily caloric requirement is \\(\\boxed{2000}\\) calories.", "To find out the total number of calories that fulfill a person's daily caloric requirement, we can set up a simple equation based on the information given.\n\nWe know that a snack-size tin of peaches has 40 calories and this is 2% of t