ac{11}{2} \\).\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{11}{2}}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure the accuracy of the result.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve, Abs\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\nx = symbols('x')\r\n\r\n# Define the equation\r\nequation = Eq(Abs(x + 5) - Abs(3*x - 6), 0)\r\n\r\n# Solve the equation\r\nsolutions = solve(equation, x)\r\nprint(solutions)\n```", "To solve the equation \\(|x+5| - |3x-6| = 0\\), we need to consider the points where the expressions inside the absolute values change their signs, i.e., \\(x = -5\\) and \\(x = 2\\). These points divide the real number line into three intervals: \\((-\\infty, -5)\\), \\([-5, 2]\\), and \\((2, \\infty)\\). We will solve the equation in each of these intervals separately.\n\n1. For \\(x < -5\\):\n   \\[\n   |x+5| = -(x+5) = -x-5 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad |3x-6| = -(3x-6) = -3x+6\n   \\]\n   So the equation becomes:\n   \\[\n   -x-5 - (-3x+6) = 0 \\implies -x-5 + 3x-6 = 0 \\implies 2x-11 = 0 \\implies x = \\frac{11}{2}\n   \\]\n   Since \\(\\frac{11}{2} \\not< -5\\), \\(x = \\frac{11}{2}\\) is not a solution in this interval.\n\n2. For \\(-5 \\leq x \\leq 2\\):\n   \\[\n   |x+5| = x+5 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad |3x-6| = -(3x-6) = -3x+6\n   \\]\n   So the equation becomes:\n   \\[\n   x+5 - (-3x+6) = 0 \\implies x+5 + 3x-6 = 0 \\implies 4x-1 = 0 \\implies x = \\frac{1}{4}\n   \\]\n   Since \\(-5 \\leq \\frac{1}{4} \\leq 2\\), \\(x = \\frac{1}{4}\\) is a solution in this interval.\n\n3. For \\(x > 2\\):\n   \\[\n   |x+5| = x+5 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad |3x-6| = 3x-6\n   \\]\n   So the equation becomes:\n   \\[\n   x+5 - (3x-6) = 0 \\implies x+5 - 3x+6 = 0 \\implies -2x+11 = 0 \\implies x = \\frac{11}{2}\n   \\]\n   Since \\(\\frac{11}{2} > 2\\), \\(x = \\frac{11}{2}\\) is a solution in this interval.\n\nAmong the solutions \\(x = \\frac{1}{4}\\) and \\(x = \\frac{11}{2}\\), the largest possible value of \\(x\\) is \\(\\frac{11}{2}\\).\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{11}{2}}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure the accuracy of the result.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve, Abs\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\nx = symbols('x')\r\n\r\n# Define the equation\r\nequation = Eq(Abs(x + 5) - Abs(3*x - 6), 0)\r\n\r\n# Solve the equation\r\nsolutions = solve(equation, x)\r\n\r\n# Filter the solutions to find the largest possible value\r\nvalid_solutions = [sol.evalf() for sol in solutions if sol.is_real]\r\nmax_solution = max(valid_solutions)\r\n\r\nprint(max_solution)\n```", 'If $|2x-1|=|3x+2|$, find the largest possible value of $x$. Express your answer as an improper fraction. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}.