 = n % 5\n        base5_number = str(remainder) + base5_number\n        n = n // 5\n    \n    return base5_number\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase5_number = decimal_to_base5(decimal_number)\nprint(base5_number)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe decimal number \\(555_{10}\\) expressed in base 5 is \\(\\boxed{4210_5}\\).', 'To convert a decimal number to base 5, we repeatedly divide the number by 5 and keep track of the remainders. The conversion process can be summarized as follows:\n\n1. Divide the number by 5.\n2. Record the remainder.\n3. Update the number to the quotient from the division.\n4. Repeat steps 1-3 until the quotient is 0.\n5. The base 5 number is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top.\n\nLet\'s convert $555_{10}$ to base 5 using Python.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base_5(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    \n    base_5_digits = []\n    \n    while n > 0:\n        remainder = n % 5\n        base_5_digits.append(str(remainder))\n        n = n // 5\n    \n    # The base 5 number is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top\n    base_5_digits.reverse()\n    return \'\'.join(base_5_digits)\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\nbase_5_number = decimal_to_base_5(555)\nprint(base_5_number)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base 5 representation of the decimal number $555_{10}$ is $\\boxed{4210_5}$.', 'To convert a decimal number to base 5, we need to repeatedly divide the number by 5 and keep track of the remainders. The conversion process involves the following steps:\n\n1. Divide the number by 5.\n2. Record the remainder.\n3. Update the number to the quotient of the division.\n4. Repeat steps 1-3 until the quotient is 0.\n5. The base 5 number is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top.\n\nLet\'s convert the decimal number 555 to base 5 using Python code.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base5(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    \n    base5 = ""\n    while n > 0:\n        remainder = n % 5\n        base5 = str(remainder) + base5\n        n = n // 5\n    \n    return base5\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase5_number = decimal_to_base5(decimal_number)\nprint(base5_number)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base 5 representation of the decimal number 555 is \\(\\boxed{4210_5}\\).', 'To convert a decimal number to a different base, we repeatedly divide the number by the base and keep track of the remainders. The remainders, read in reverse order, give the number in the new base. Let\'s convert \\(555_{10}\\) to base 5 using Python.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base(n, base):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % base))\n        n //= base\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase = 5\nbase_5_number = decimal_to_base(decimal_number, base)\nprint(base_5_number)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe decimal number \\(555_{10}\\) is equivalent to \\(4210_5\\) in base 5. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{4210_5}\\)', 'To convert a decimal number to another base, we repeatedly divide the number by the new base and keep track of the remainders. The conversion process for $555_{10}$ to base $5$ is as follows:\n\n1. Divide 555 by 5. The quotient is 111 and the remainder is 0.\n2. Divide 111 by 5. The quotient is 22 and the remainder is 1.\n3. Divide 22 by 5. The quotient is 4 and the remainder is 2.\n4. Divide 4 by 5. The quotient is 0 and the remainder is 4.\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get the base 5 representation of 555. Let\'s write the code to perform this conversion.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base(n, base):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % base))\n        n //= base\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase = 5\nbase_5_representation = decimal_to_base(decimal_number, base)\nprint(base_5_representation)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base 5 representation of the decimal number $555_{10}$ is $\\boxed{4210_5}$.', 'To convert the decimal number \\(555_{10}\\) to base \\(5\\), we repeatedly divide the number by \\(5\\) and keep track of the remainders. The conversion process involves the following steps:\n\n1. Divide \\(555\\) by \\(5\\) to get the quotient and remainder.\n2. Divide the quotient from the previous step by \\(5\\) to get the new quotient and remainder.\n3. Repeat the process until the quotient is \\(0\\).\n4. The base \\(5\\) representation is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top.\n\nLet\'s perform the conversion using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base5(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    \n    base5_digits = []\n    \n    while n > 0:\n        remainder = n % 5\n        base5_digits.append(str(remainder))\n        n = n // 5\n    \n    # The base 5 representation is the reverse of the collected remainders\n    base5_digits.reverse()\n    return \'\'.join(base5_digits)\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\nbase5_representation = decimal_to_base5(555)\nprint(base5_representation)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base \\(5\\) representation of \\(555_{10}\\) is \\(4210_5\\).\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{4210_5}\n\\]', 'To convert a decimal number to a different base, we repeatedly divide the number by the new base and keep track of the remainders. The conversion of \\(555_{10}\\) to base \\(5\\) can be done as follows:\n\n1. Divide 555 by 5, record the quotient and remainder.\n2. Divide the quotient from the previous step by 5, record the new quotient and remainder.\n3. Repeat this process until the quotient is 0.\n4. The base-5 representation is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top.\n\nLet\'s perform this conversion using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base(n,