the magnitude of the cross product\nmagnitude = np.linalg.norm(cross_product)\n\n# The area of the triangle is half the magnitude of the cross product\narea = 0.5 * magnitude\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n6.708203932499369\n```\nThe area of triangle \\(OAB\\) is \\(3\\sqrt{5}\\), which is approximately \\(6.708\\). Therefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]", "To find the area of triangle \\(OAB\\), we can use the cross product of vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{OA}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB}\\). The magnitude of the cross product of two vectors gives the area of the parallelogram formed by those vectors. The area of the triangle is half of this value.\n\nThe cross product of two vectors \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} u_1 \\\\ u_2 \\\\ u_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\\\ v_2 \\\\ v_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} u_2 v_3 - u_3 v_2 \\\\ u_3 v_1 - u_1 v_3 \\\\ u_1 v_2 - u_2 v_1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nThe magnitude of the cross product is:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\| = \\sqrt{(u_2 v_3 - u_3 v_2)^2 + (u_3 v_1 - u_1 v_3)^2 + (u_1 v_2 - u_2 v_1)^2}\n\\]\nThe area of the triangle is then:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\|\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\|\n\\]\nLet's calculate this step-by-step using Python.\n\nFirst, we define the vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{OA}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB}\\):\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nThen we compute the cross product:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-2) \\\\ 3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1 \\\\ 1 \\cdot (-2) - 2 \\cdot (-3) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 + 6 \\\\ -9 - 1 \\\\ -2 + 6 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nThe magnitude of this cross product is:\n\\[\n\\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\| = \\sqrt{8^2 + (-10)^2 + 4^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 100 + 16} = \\sqrt{180} = 6\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\nSo the area of the triangle \\(OAB\\) is:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 6\\sqrt{5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Define the vectors OA and OB\nOA = np.array([1, 2, 3])\nOB = np.array([-3, -2, 1])\n\n# Compute the cross product of OA and OB\ncross_product = np.cross(OA, OB)\n\n# Compute the magnitude of the cross product\nmagnitude = np.linalg.norm(cross_product)\n\n# Compute the area of the triangle OAB\narea = 0.5 * magnitude\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n6.708203932499369\n```\nThe area of triangle \\(OAB\\) is \\(3\\sqrt{5}\\), which is approximately \\(6.708\\). Therefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]", "To find the area of triangle \\(OAB\\), we can use the fact that the area of a triangle formed by two vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{OA}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB}\\) is half the magnitude of the cross product of these two vectors. The cross product \\(\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\) gives a vector whose magnitude is equal to the area of the parallelogram formed by \\(\\overrightarrow{OA}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB}\\). Therefore, the area of triangle \\(OAB\\) is half of this magnitude.\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe cross product \\(\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\) is calculated as follows:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{vmatrix}\n\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\\n1 & 2 & 3 \\\\\n-3 & -2 & 1\n\\end{vmatrix}\n= \\mathbf{i}(2 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-2)) - \\mathbf{j}(1 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-3)) + \\mathbf{k}(1 \\cdot (-2) - 2 \\cdot (-3))\n= \\mathbf{i}(2 + 6) - \\mathbf{j}(1 + 9) + \\mathbf{k}(-2 