n\\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\| = \\sqrt{8^2 + (-10)^2 + 4^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 100 + 16} = \\sqrt{180} = 6\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nThe area of triangle $OAB$ is half of this magnitude:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 6\\sqrt{5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Define the vectors OA and OB\nOA = np.array([1, 2, 3])\nOB = np.array([-3, -2, 1])\n\n# Calculate the cross product of OA and OB\ncross_product = np.cross(OA, OB)\n\n# Calculate the magnitude of the cross product\nmagnitude = np.linalg.norm(cross_product)\n\n# The area of the triangle is half the magnitude of the cross product\narea = 0.5 * magnitude\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n6.708203932499369\n```\nThe calculated area of triangle $OAB$ is approximately $6.708$, which matches $3\\sqrt{5}$ when evaluated numerically. Therefore, the exact area of triangle $OAB$ is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{3\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]", "To find the area of triangle \\(OAB\\), we can use the fact that the area of a triangle formed by two vectors \\(\\mathbf{u}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v}\\) is given by half the magnitude of the cross product of the two vectors. The vectors \\(\\mathbf{u}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v}\\) are \\(\\overrightarrow{OA}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB}\\), respectively.\n\nThe steps are as follows:\n\n1. Compute the cross product of \\(\\overrightarrow{OA}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB}\\).\n2. Find the magnitude of the cross product.\n3. Divide the magnitude by 2 to get the area of the triangle.\n\nLet's do this step-by-step using Python.\n\nFirst, we define the vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{OA}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB}\\):\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe cross product \\(\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{vmatrix}