qrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}\\) is indeed \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\).\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\n\\]", "To simplify the expression \\(\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}\\), we can break it down step by step.\n\n1. Start with the innermost expression: \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}\\).\n2. Simplify the square root of \\(\\frac{1}{729}\\).\n3. Take the cube root of the result from step 2.\n4. Finally, take the square root of the result from step 3.\n\nLet's go through these steps using Python to ensure accuracy.\n\nFirst, we note that \\(729 = 3^6\\), so \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3^6}} = \\frac{1}{3^3} = \\frac{1}{27}\\).\n\nNext, we take the cube root of \\(\\frac{1}{27}\\), which is \\(\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{1}{27}} = \\frac{1}{3}\\).\n\nFinally, we take the square root of \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\), which is \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\).\n\nTo rationalize the denominator, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by \\(\\sqrt{3}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{1 \\cdot \\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n\\]\n\nSo, the final answer is \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\).\n\nLet's verify this step-by-step using Python.\n```python\nfrom sympy import sqrt, Rational\r\n\r\n# Innermost expression\r\ninnermost = Rational(1, 729)\r\n\r\n# Square root of the innermost expression\r\nsqrt_innermost = sqrt(innermost)\r\n\r\n# Cube root of the result from the previous step\r\ncube_root = sqrt_innermost**(Rational(1, 3))\r\n\r\n# Square root of the result from the previous step\r\nfinal_result = sqrt(cube_root)\r\n\r\n# Rationalize the denominator\r\nrationalized_result = final_result * sqrt(3) / sqrt(3)\r\n\r\nprint(rationalized_result.simplify())\n```\n```output\nsqrt(3)/3\n```\nThe final simplified result of the expression \\(\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\\).", "To simplify the expression \\(\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\fr