n\nThus, the probability that Alice wins the game is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{2}{3}}\\).", "To find the remainder when the polynomial $(5x + 9)^{611} + (x + 5)^{11} + (x - 1)^{11} + 3x^2 + 1$ is divided by $x + 2$, we can use the Remainder Theorem. The Remainder Theorem states that the remainder of the division of a polynomial $f(x)$ by a linear divisor $x - c$ is $f(c)$. In this case, the divisor is $x + 2$, so we need to find the value of the polynomial when $x = -2$.\n\nLet's substitute $x = -2$ into the polynomial and evaluate it:\n\n\\[\nf(x) = (5x + 9)^{611} + (x + 5)^{11} + (x - 1)^{11} + 3x^2 + 1\n\\]\n\n\\[\nf(-2) = (5(-2) + 9)^{611} + (-2 + 5)^{11} + (-2 - 1)^{11} + 3(-2)^2 + 1\n\\]\n\n\\[\nf(-2) = (-10 + 9)^{611} + 3^{11} + (-3)^{11} + 3(4) + 1\n\\]\n\n\\[\nf(-2) = (-1)^{611} + 3^{11} + (-3)^{11} + 12 + 1\n\\]\n\nSince $(-1)^{611} = -1$ (because 611 is an odd number), and $(-3)^{11} = -3^{11}$ (because 11 is an odd number), we can simplify further:\n\n\\[\nf(-2) = -1 + 3^{11} - 3^{11} + 12 + 1\n\\]\n\n\\[\nf(-2) = -1 + 0 + 12 + 1\n\\]\n\n\\[\nf(-2) = 12\n\\]\n\nSo the remainder when $(5x + 9)^{611} + (x + 5)^{11} + (x - 1)^{11} + 3x^2 + 1$ is divided by $x + 2$ is $12$. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the polynomial function\r\ndef polynomial(x):\r\n    return (5 * x + 9)**611 + (x + 5)**11 + (x - 1)**11 + 3 * x**2 + 1\r\n\r\n# Evaluate the polynomial at x = -2\r\nremainder = polynomial(-2)\r\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n12\n```\nThe remainder when $(5x + 9)^{611} + (x + 5)^{11} + (x - 1)^{11} + 3x^2 + 1$ is divided by $x + 2$ is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).", "To find the remainder when the polynomial \\(P(x) = (5x + 9)^{611} + (x + 5)^{11} + (x - 1)^{11} + 3x^2 + 1\\) is divided by \\(x + 2\\), we can use the Remainder Theorem. According to the Remainder Theorem, the remainder of the division of a polynomial \\(P(x)\\) by \\(x - c\\) is \\(P(c)\\). In this case, we need to find \\(P(-2)\\).\n\nLet's substitute \\(x = -2\\) into the polynomial \\(P(x)\\):\n\n\\[\nP(-2) = (5(-2) + 9)^{611} + ((-2) + 5)^{11} + ((-2) - 1)^{11} + 3(-2)^2 + 1\n\\]\n\nSimplifying each term:\n\n\\[\n5(-2) + 9 = -10 + 9 = -1 \\implies (-1)^{611} = -1\n\\]\n\n\\[\n(-2) + 5 = 3 \\implies 3^{11}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n(-2) - 1 = -3 \\implies (-3)^{11} = -3^{11}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n3(-2)^2 = 3(4) = 12\n\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\n\\[\nP(-2) = -1 + 3^{11} - 3^{11} + 12 + 1 = -1 + 12 + 1 = 12\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when \\(P(x)\\) is divided by \\(x + 2\\) is \\(12\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the polynomial function P(x)\ndef P(x):\n    return (5 * x + 9)**611 + (x + 5)**11 + (x - 1)**11 + 3 * x**2 + 1\n\n# Calculate P(-2)\nremainder = P(-2)\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n12\n```\nThe remainder when the polynomial \\( (5x + 9)^{611} + (x + 5)^{11} + (x - 1)^{11} + 3x^2 + 1 \\) is divided by \\( x + 2 \\) is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).", "To find the remainder when the polynomial \\(P(x) = (5x + 9)^{611} + (x + 5)^{11} + (x - 1)^{11} + 3x^2 + 1\\) is divided by \\(x + 2\\), we can use the Remainder Theorem. The Remainder Theorem states that the remainder of the division of a polynomial \\(P(x)\\) by \\(x - c\\) is \\(P(c)\\). In this case, we need to find \\(P(-2)\\).\n\nLet's break down the polynomial and evaluate it at \\(x = -2\\):\n\n1. Evaluate \\((5x + 9)^{611}\\) at \\(x = -2\\):\n   \\[\n   (5(-2) + 9)^{611} = (-10 + 9)^{611} = (-1)^{611} = -1\n   \\]\n\n2. Evaluate \\((x + 5)^{11}\\) at \\(x = -2\\):\n   \\[\n   (-2 + 5)^{11} = 3^{11}\n   \\]\n\n3. Evaluate \\((x - 1)^{11}\\) at \\(x = -2\\):\n   \\[\n   (-2 - 1)^{11} = (-3)^{11} = -3^{11}\n   \\]\n\n4. Evaluate \\(3x^2\\) at \\(x = -2\\):\n   \\[\n   3(-2)^2 = 3 \\cdot 4 = 12\n   \\]\n\n5. Evaluate the constant term \\(1\\) at \\(x = -2\\):\n   \\[\n   1\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all these values to find \\(P(-2)\\):\n\\[\nP(-2) = -1 + 3^{11} - 3^{11} + 12 + 1 = -1 + 0 + 12 + 1 = 12\n\\]\n\nSo, the remainder when \\(P(x)\\) is divided by \\(x + 2\\) is \\(12\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the polynomial function P(x)\ndef P(x):\n    return (5*x + 9)**611 + (x + 5)**11 + (x - 1)**11 + 3*x**2 + 1\n\n# Evaluate the polynomial at x = -2\nremainder = P(-2)\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n12\n```\nThe remainder when the polynomial \\( (5x + 9)^{611} + (x + 5)^{11} + (x - 1)^{11} + 3x^2 + 1 \\) is divided by \\( x + 2 \\) is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).", "To find the remainder when a polynomial \\( P(x) \\) is divided by \\( x + 2 \\), we can use the Remainder Theorem. The Remainder Theorem states that the remainder of the division of a polynomial \\( P(x) \\) by \\( x - c \\) is \\( P(c) \\). In this case, we are dividing by \\( x + 2 \\), which is the same as \\( x - (-2) \\), so we need to find \\( P(-2) \\).\n\nGiven the polynomial:\n\\[ P(x) = (5x + 9)^{611} + (x + 5)^{11} + (x - 1)^{11} + 3x^2 + 1 \\]\n\nWe need to evaluate \\( P(-2) \\):\n\\[ P(-2) = (5(-2) + 9)^{611} + (-2 + 5)^{11} + (-2 - 1)^{11} + 3(-2)^2 + 1 \\]\n\nLet's break this down step by step:\n1. Calculate \\( 5(-2) + 9 \\):\n\\[ 5(-2) + 9 = -10 + 9 = -1 \\]\nSo, \\( (5(-2) + 9)^{611} = (-1)^{611} \\). Since 611 is an odd number, \\( (-1)^{611} = -1 \\).\n\n2. Calculate \\( -2 + 5 \\):\n\\[ -2 + 5 = 3 \\]\nSo, \\( (-2 + 5)^{11} = 3^{11} \\).\n\n3. Calculate \\( -2 - 1 \\):\n\\[ -2 - 1 = -3 \\]\nSo, \\( (-2 - 1)^{11} = (-3)^{11} \\). Since 11 is an odd number, \\( (-3)^{11} = -3^{11} \\).\n\n4. Calculate \\( 3(-2)^2 \\):\n\\[ 3(-2)^2 = 3(4) = 12 \\]\n\nSo, the expression becomes:\n\\[ P(-2) = -1 + 3^{11} - 3^{11} + 12 + 1 \\]\n\nNotice that \\( 3^{11} \\) and \\( -3^{11} \\) cancel each other out:\n\\[ P(-2) = -1 + 12 + 1 = 12 \\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when \\( (5x + 9)^{611} + (x + 5)^{11} + (x - 1)^{11} + 3x^2 + 1 \\) is divided by \\( x + 2 \\) is \\( \\boxed{12} \\).\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure the accuracy of the result.\n```python\n# Define the polynomial function P(x)\ndef P(x):\n    return (5*x +