e equation was handled. Let's correct the approach and ensure we properly extract the coefficients for \\(m\\) and \\(b\\).\n\nHere's the corrected code:\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\n\n# Define the symbols\nt, x, y = symbols('t x y')\n\n# Define the parameterized equations\nx_eq = Eq(x, 8 + 2*t)\ny_eq = Eq(y, -1 + 3*t)\n\n# Solve the x equation for t\nt_expr = solve(x_eq, t)[0]\n\n# Substitute t into the y equation\ny_expr = y_eq.subs(t, t_expr)\n\n# Simplify the equation to the form y = mx + b\ny_expr_simplified = y_expr.rhs.expand()\nm = y_expr_simplified.coeff(x)\nb = y_expr_simplified - m*x\n\nprint(((m, b)))\n```\n```output\n(3/2, -13)\n```\nThe ordered pair \\((m, b)\\) representing the slope and y-intercept of the line is \\(\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, -13\\right)\\).\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, -13\\right)}\n\\]", "To find the equation of the line in the form \\( y = mx + b \\) from the given parameterized line, we need to eliminate the parameter \\( t \\) and express \\( y \\) in terms of \\( x \\).\n\nGiven the parameterized line:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} + t \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nThis can be written as two separate equations:\n\\[\nx = 8 + 2t\n\\]\n\\[\ny = -1 + 3t\n\\]\n\nFirst, solve the equation for \\( x \\) to express \\( t \\) in terms of \\( x \\):\n\\[\nx = 8 + 2t \\implies 2t = x - 8 \\implies t = \\frac{x - 8}{2}\n\\]\n\nNow substitute this expression for \\( t \\) into the equation for \\( y \\):\n\\[\ny = -1 + 3\\left(\\frac{x - 8}{2}\\right) = -1 + \\frac{3x - 24}{2} = -1 + \\frac{3x}{2} - 12 = \\frac{3x}{2} - 13\n\\]\n\nThus, the equation of the line is:\n\\[\ny = \\frac{3}{2}x - 13\n\\]\n\nSo, the ordered pair \\((m, b)\\) is \\(\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, -13\\right)\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\n\n# Define the symbols\nt, x,