) and \\(b\\), the horizontal distance is \\(\\frac{|c - d|}{|a - b|}\\). Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\left| \\frac{c - d}{a - b} \\right| \\cdot |c - d| = \\left| \\frac{(c - d)^2}{a - b} \\right| = 18.\n   \\]\n   Since \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) are positive integers, we can assume \\(a > b\\) without loss of generality, so the equation becomes:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(c - d)^2}{a - b} = 18.\n   \\]\n\n2. **Area of the Second Parallelogram:**\n   Similarly, the area of the second parallelogram bounded by the lines \\(y = ax + c\\), \\(y = ax - d\\), \\(y = bx + c\\), and \\(y = bx - d\\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\left| \\frac{c + d}{a - b} \\right| \\cdot |c + d| = \\left| \\frac{(c + d)^2}{a - b} \\right| = 72.\n   \\]\n   Again, since \\(a > b\\), the equation becomes:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(c + d)^2}{a - b} = 72.\n   \\]\n\n3. **Solving the Equations:**\n   We now have two equations:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(c - d)^2}{a - b} = 18,\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(c + d)^2}{a - b} = 72.\n   \\]\n   Dividing the second equation by the first, we get:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(c + d)^2}{(c - d)^2} = 4.\n   \\]\n   Taking the square root of both sides, we get:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{c + d}{c - d} = 2 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad \\frac{c + d}{c - d} = -2.\n   \\]\n   Since \\(c\\) and \\(d\\) are positive integers, we can discard the negative solution, so:\n   \\[\n   c + d = 2(c - d).\n   \\]\n   Simplifying, we get:\n   \\[\n   c + d = 2c - 2d \\implies 3d = c.\n   \\]\n   Substituting \\(c = 3d\\) into the first equation, we get:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(3d - d)^2}{a - b} = 18 \\implies \\frac{(2d)^2}{a - b} = 18 \\implies \\frac{4d^2}{a - b} = 18 \\implies 4d^2 = 18(a - b) \\implies 2d^2 = 9(a - b).\n   \\]\n   Therefore, \\(a - b = \\frac{2d^2}{9}\\). Since \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are integers, \\(2d^2\\) must be divisible by 9, so \\(d\\) must be a multiple of 3. The smallest possible value for \\(d\\) is 3. Substituting \\(d = 3\\), w