enominator by 11, we get:\n\n\\[ \\frac{1331 \\div 11}{9999 \\div 11} = \\frac{121}{909} \\]\n\nSince 121 and 909 have no common divisors other than 1 (i.e., they are coprime), the fraction \\(\\frac{121}{909}\\) is in its simplest form. Therefore, \\(a = 121\\) and \\(b = 909\\), and the sum \\(a + b = 121 + 909 = 1030\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1030}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nfrom math import gcd\n\n# Values of the numerator and denominator\nnumerator = 1331\ndenominator = 9999\n\n# Calculate the greatest common divisor\ncommon_divisor = gcd(numerator, denominator)\n\n# Simplify the fraction\nsimplified_numerator = numerator // common_divisor\nsimplified_denominator = denominator // common_divisor\n\n# Calculate the sum of the simplified numerator and denominator\nresult = simplified_numerator + simplified_denominator\nprint(result)\n```", "To convert the repeating decimal \\(0.\\overline{1331}\\) into a fraction, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Let \\( x = 0.\\overline{1331} \\).\n2. Multiply \\( x \\) by 10000 (since the repeating part is 4 digits long), so \\( 10000x = 1331.\\overline{1331} \\).\n3. Subtract the original \\( x \\) from this equation: \\( 10000x - x = 1331.\\overline{1331} - 0.\\overline{1331} \\).\n4. This simplifies to \\( 9999x = 1331 \\), so \\( x = \\frac{1331}{9999} \\).\n5. Simplify the fraction \\( \\frac{1331}{9999} \\) by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 1331 and 9999. The GCD of 1331 and 9999 is 11, so \\( \\frac{1331}{9999} = \\frac{121}{909} \\).\n6. The fraction \\( \\frac{121}{909} \\) is in its simplest form, so \\( a = 121 \\) and \\( b = 909 \\).\n7. The sum \\( a + b = 121 + 909 = 1030 \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nfrom math import gcd\n\n# Values for the fraction\nnumerator = 1331\ndenominator = 9999\n\n# Calculate the greatest common divisor\ncommon_divisor = gcd(numerator, denominator)\n\n# Simplify 