s:\n\n1. Let \\(\\sqrt{120-\\sqrt{x}} = k\\), where \\(k\\) is an integer.\n2. Then, \\(120 - \\sqrt{x} = k^2\\).\n3. Rearrange to solve for \\(\\sqrt{x}\\): \\(\\sqrt{x} = 120 - k^2\\).\n4. Since \\(\\sqrt{x}\\) must be a non-negative real number, \\(120 - k^2 \\geq 0\\).\n5. This implies \\(k^2 \\leq 120\\).\n6. The largest integer \\(k\\) that satisfies this inequality is \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{120} \\rfloor = 10\\), and the smallest integer \\(k\\) is 0.\n7. Therefore, \\(k\\) can take any integer value from 0 to 10, inclusive. This gives us 11 possible values for \\(k\\).\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Calculate the number of integer values for k such that 0 <= k^2 <= 120\nimport math\n\n# The maximum value of k is the floor of the square root of 120\nmax_k = math.isqrt(120)  # This gives the integer part of the square root of 120\n\n# The possible values for k range from 0 to max_k, inclusive\npossible_k_values = list(range(max_k + 1))\n\n# The number of possible values for k\nnumber_of_possible_values = len(possible_k_values)\nprint(number_of_possible_values)\n```\n```output\n11\n```\nThe number of real values of \\( x \\) for which \\(\\sqrt{120 - \\sqrt{x}}\\) is an integer is \\(\\boxed{11}\\).", "To determine the number of real values of \\(x\\) for which \\(\\sqrt{120 - \\sqrt{x}}\\) is an integer, we can proceed as follows:\n\n1. Let \\( \\sqrt{120 - \\sqrt{x}} = k \\), where \\( k \\) is an integer.\n2. Then, \\( 120 - \\sqrt{x} = k^2 \\).\n3. Rearrange to find \\( \\sqrt{x} \\): \\( \\sqrt{x} = 120 - k^2 \\).\n4. Since \\( \\sqrt{x} \\) must be non-negative, \\( 120 - k^2 \\geq 0 \\). This implies \\( k^2 \\leq 120 \\).\n5. The largest integer \\( k \\) can be is \\( \\lfloor \\sqrt{120} \\rfloor = 10 \\). The smallest integer \\( k \\) can be is 0.\n6. Therefore, \\( k \\) can take any integer value from 0 to 10, inclusive. This gives us 11 possible values for \\( k \\).\n\nThus, there are 11 real values of \\( x 