 1723, 1850, 1977, 2102, 2227, 2352, 2477, 2602, 2727, 2852, 2977, 3102, 3227, 3352, 3477] \\]\n\nGiven the periodicity, we can find the values of \\(x_{531}\\), \\(x_{753}\\), and \\(x_{975}\\) by reducing the indices modulo 4:\n\n- \\(531 \\mod 4 = 3\\), so \\(x_{531} = x_3 = 420\\)\n- \\(753 \\mod 4 = 1\\), so \\(x_{753} = x_1 = 211\\)\n- \\(975 \\mod 4 = 3\\), so \\(x_{975} = x_3 = 420\\)\n\nThus, \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975} = 420 + 211 + 420 = 1051\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1051}\n\\]", "To solve this problem, we need to compute the sequence \\(x_n\\) for \\(n \\geq 5\\) using the given recurrence relation \\(x_n = x_{n-1} - x_{n-2} + x_{n-3} - x_{n-4}\\). We will then find the values of \\(x_{531}\\), \\(x_{753}\\), and \\(x_{975}\\) and sum them up.\n\nFirst, let's write a Python function to generate the sequence up to the required indices. We'll then compute the values of \\(x_{531}\\), \\(x_{753}\\), and \\(x_{975}\\) and find their sum.\n\nHere is the Python code to solve the problem:\n```python\n# Define the initial values\nx = [211, 375, 420, 523]\n\n# Generate the sequence up to the required indices\nfor n in range(4, 1000):  # We go up to 1000 to ensure we have enough terms\n    x_n = x[n-1] - x[n-2] + x[n-3] - x[n-4]\n    x.append(x_n)\n\n# Find the values of x_531, x_753, and x_975\nx_531 = x[530]\nx_753 = x[752]\nx_975 = x[974]\n\n# Calculate the sum\nresult = x_531 + x_753 + x_975\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n898\n```\nThe value of \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\) is \\(\\boxed{898}\\).", "To find the value of \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\), we need to analyze the recurrence relation \\(x_n = x_{n-1} - x_{n-2} + x_{n-3} - x_{n-4}\\) for \\(n \\geq 5\\). Given the initial conditions \\(x_1 = 211\\), \\(x_2 = 375\\), \\(x_3 = 420\\), and \\(x_4 = 523\\), we can generate the sequence and observe if there is any periodicity.\n\nLet's compute the first few terms of the sequence to identify any patterns:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nx_5 &= x_4 - x_3 + x_2 - x_1 = 523 - 420 + 375 - 211 = 267, \\\\\nx_6 &= x_5 - x_4 + x_3 - x_2 = 267 - 523 + 420 - 375 = -211, \\\\\nx_7 &= x_6 - x_5 + x_4 - x_3 = -211 - 267 + 523 - 420 = -375, \\\\\nx_8 &= x_7 - x_6 + x_5 - x_4 = -375 - (-211) + 267 - 523 = -420, \\\\\nx_9 &= x_8 - x_7 + x_6 - x_5 = -420 - (-375) + (-211) - 267 = -523, \\\\\nx_{10} &= x_9 - x_8 + x_7 - x_6 = -523 - (-420) + (-375) - (-211) = -267, \\\\\nx_{11} &= x_{10} - x_9 + x_8 - x_7 = -267 - (-523) + (-420) - (-375) = 211, \\\\\nx_{12} &= x_{11} - x_{10} + x_9 - x_8 = 211 - (-267) + (-523) - (-420) = 375.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nWe can see that \\(x_{11} = x_1\\) and \\(x_{12} = x_2\\). This suggests that the sequence is periodic with a period of 10. Therefore, \\(x_{n} = x_{n \\mod 10}\\).\n\nNow, we can find \\(x_{531}\\), \\(x_{753}\\), and \\(x_{975}\\) by reducing these indices modulo 10:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n531 \\mod 10 &= 1, \\\\\n753 \\mod 10 &= 3, \\\\\n975 \\mod 10 &= 5.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nSo, \\(x_{531} = x_1 = 211\\), \\(x_{753} = x_3 = 420\\), and \\(x_{975} = x_5 = 267\\). Therefore,\n\n\\[\nx_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975} = 211 + 420 + 267 = 898.\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this by implementing the solution in Python.\n```python\n# Initial conditions\nx = [211, 375, 420, 523]\n\n# Generate the sequence up to the 10th term to confirm the periodicity\nfor n in range(4, 10):\n    x.append(x[n-1] - x[n-2] + x[n-3] - x[n-4])\n\n# The sequence is periodic with a period of 10\nperiod = 10\n\n# Find x_531, x_753, and x_975\nx_531 = x[531 % period - 1]\nx_753 = x[753 % period - 1]\nx_975 = x[975 % period - 1]\n\n# Calculate the sum\nresult = x_531 + x_753 + x_975\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n898\n```\nThe value of \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\) is \\(\\boxed{898}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to first understand the recurrence relation and then compute the values of the sequence up to the required terms. The recurrence relation given is:\n\n\\[x_n = x_{n-1} - x_{n-2} + x_{n-3} - x_{n-4} \\text{ for } n \\geq 5.\\]\n\nWe are given the initial values:\n\\[x_1 = 211, \\quad x_2 = 375, \\quad x_3 = 420, \\quad x_4 = 523.\\]\n\nWe will use these initial values to compute the subsequent terms of the sequence. Let's write a Python function to compute the terms of the sequence and then find the values of \\(x_{531}\\), \\(x_{753}\\), and \\(x_{975}\\). Finally, we will sum these values.\n\nLet's implement this in Python.\n```python\ndef compute_sequence(n):\n    # Initial values\n    x = [211, 375, 420, 523]\n    \n    # Compute the sequence up to the nth term\n    for i in range(4, n):\n        next_term = x[i-1] - x[i-2] + x[i-3] - x[i-4]\n        x.append(next_term)\n    \n    return x\n\n# Compute the sequence up to the 975th term\nsequence = compute_sequence(975)\n\n# Extract the required terms\nx_531 = sequence[530]\nx_753 = sequence[752]\nx_975 = sequence[974]\n\n# Compute the sum\nresult = x_531 + x_753 + x_975\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n898\n```\nThe value of \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\) is \\(\\boxed{898}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to understand the recursive sequence given by:\n\\[ x_n = x_{n-1} - x_{n-2} + x_{n-3} - x_{n-4} \\]\nfor \\( n \\geq 5 \\), with the initial conditions \\( x_1 = 211 \\), \\( x_2 = 375 \\), \\( x_3 = 420 \\), and \\( x_4 = 523 \\).\n\nFirst, we will generate the sequence up to a point where we can identify any repeating patterns. We can then use this pattern to find the values of \\( x_{531} \\), \\( x_{753} \\), and \\( x_{975} \\).\n\nLet's start by computing the first few terms of the sequence:\n\\[ x_5 = x_4 - x_3 + x_2 - x_1 = 523 - 420 + 375 - 211 = 267 \\]\n\\[ x_6 = x_5 - x_4 + x_3 - x_2 = 267 - 523 + 420 - 375 = -211 \\]\n\\[ x_7 = x_6 - x_5 + x_4 - x_3 = -211 - 267 + 523 - 420 = -375 \\]\n\\[ x_8 = x_7 - x_6 + x_5 - x_4 = -375 - (-211) + 267 - 523 = -420 \\]\n\\[ x_9 = x_8 - x_7 + x_6 - x_5 = -420 - (-375) + (-211) - 267 = -523 \\]\n\\[ x_{10} = x_9 - x_8 + x_7 - x_6 = -523 - 