s by their respective prices.\n3. Sum up the total cost for all the stamps from the 1970s.\n4. Divide the total cost by the total number of stamps to get the average price.\n\nFrom the table, we can see that:\n- In the 1970s, Juan had 12 stamps from Brazil, 12 stamps from France, 6 stamps from Peru, and 13 stamps from Spain.\n- The price for stamps from Brazil and Peru is 6 cents each.\n- The price for stamps from France and Spain is 5 cents each.\n\nNow we can calculate the total cost for the 1970s stamps:\n\\[ \\text{Total cost} = (12 \\times 6) + (12 \\times 5) + (6 \\times 6) + (13 \\times 5) \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the total number of stamps from the 1970s:\n\\[ \\text{Total number of stamps} = 12 + 12 + 6 + 13 = 43 \\]\n\nFinally, we can find the average price per stamp:\n\\[ \\text{Average price} = \\frac{\\text{Total cost}}{\\text{Total number of stamps}} \\]\n\nLet\'s calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Number of stamps from each country in the 1970s\nbrazil_stamps_70s = 12\nfrance_stamps_70s = 12\nperu_stamps_70s = 6\nspain_stamps_70s = 13\n\n# Prices of stamps\nprice_brazil = 6\nprice_france = 5\nprice_peru = 6\nprice_spain = 5\n\n# Calculate the total cost for the 1970s stamps\ntotal_cost_70s = (brazil_stamps_70s * price_brazil) + (france_stamps_70s * price_france) + (peru_stamps_70s * price_peru) + (spain_stamps_70s * price_spain)\n\n# Calculate the total number of stamps from the 1970s\ntotal_stamps_70s = brazil_stamps_70s + france_stamps_70s + peru_stamps_70s + spain_stamps_70s\n\n# Calculate the average price per stamp\naverage_price_70s = total_cost_70s / total_stamps_70s\n\n# Round the average price to the nearest tenth of a cent\naverage_price_70s_rounded = round(average_price_70s, 1)\nprint(average_price_70s_rounded)\n```\n```output\n5.4\n```\nThe average price of Juan\'s stamps from the 1970s, rounded to the nearest tenth of a cent, is \\(\\boxed{5.4}\\) cents.', "To find the average price of Juan's stamps from the 19