f(x) \\) to get \\( f(q(1)) \\).\n3. Set \\( f(q(1)) \\) equal to \\(-3\\) and solve for \\( b \\).\n\nLet's start by substituting \\( x = 1 \\) into \\( q(x) \\):\n\\[ q(1) = b \\cdot 1 + 1 = b + 1 \\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( q(1) \\) into \\( f(x) \\):\n\\[ f(q(1)) = f(b + 1) = (b + 1) - 3 = b - 2 \\]\n\nWe know that \\( f(q(1)) = -3 \\), so we can set up the equation:\n\\[ b - 2 = -3 \\]\n\nNow, we solve for \\( b \\):\n\\[ b = -3 + 2 \\]\n\\[ b = -1 \\]\n\nLet's confirm this by implementing it in Python.\n```python\n# Define the functions f and q\ndef f(x):\n    return x - 3\n\ndef q(x, b):\n    return b * x + 1\n\n# Given that f(q(1)) = -3, we need to find b\nx = 1\ntarget_value = -3\n\n# Calculate q(1)\nq_1 = q(x, b=0)  # We start with b=0 and will iterate to find the correct b\n\n# Calculate f(q(1))\nf_q_1 = f(q_1)\n\n# Iterate to find the correct b\nfor b in range(-10, 10):  # We assume b is within this range for simplicity\n    q_1 = q(x, b)\n    f_q_1 = f(q_1)\n    if f_q_1 == target_value:\n        result = b\n        break\n\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n-1\n```\nThe value of \\( b \\) that satisfies the equation \\( f(q(1)) = -3 \\) is \\(\\boxed{-1}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to find the value of \\(b\\) given the functions \\(f(x) = x - 3\\) and \\(q(x) = bx + 1\\) and the condition \\(f(q(1)) = -3\\).\n\nLet's break down the problem step-by-step:\n\n1. First, we need to find \\(q(1)\\). Since \\(q(x) = bx + 1\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   q(1) = b \\cdot 1 + 1 = b + 1\n   \\]\n\n2. Next, we need to find \\(f(q(1))\\). Since \\(f(x) = x - 3\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   f(q(1)) = f(b + 1) = (b + 1) - 3 = b + 1 - 3 = b - 2\n   \\]\n\n3. According to the problem, \\(f(q(1)) = -3\\). So we can set up the equation:\n   \\[\n   b - 2 = -3\n   \\]\n\n4. Solving for \\(b\\):\n   \\[\n   b = -3 + 2 = -1\n   \\]\n\nSo the value of \\(b\\) is \\(-1\\).\n\nLet's confirm this by implementing the steps in Python.\n```python\n# Define the functions f and q\nde