rt binomial\n\n# Total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14 people\ntotal_ways = binomial(14, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose 5 Republicans from 8 Republicans\nways_all_republicans = binomial(8, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose 5 Democrats from 6 Democrats\nways_all_democrats = binomial(6, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party\nways_at_least_one_from_each_party = total_ways - ways_all_republicans - ways_all_democrats\n\nprint(ways_at_least_one_from_each_party)\n```\n```output\n1940\n```\nThe number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats such that the subcommittee includes at least one member from each party is \\(\\boxed{1940}\\).", "To solve the problem of forming a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party, we can use the principle of complementary counting. We will first calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members from the 14 senators, and then subtract the number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Republicans or all Democrats.\n\n1. Calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14 senators.\n2. Calculate the number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Republicans.\n3. Calculate the number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Democrats.\n4. Subtract the sum of the number of ways to choose all Republicans and all Democrats from the total number of ways to get the number of ways to choose a subcommittee with at least one member from each party.\n\nLet's implement this in Python using the `math.comb` function to calculate combinations.\n\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14 senators\ntotal_ways = math.comb(14, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Republicans\nall_republicans = math.comb(8, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Democrats\nall_democrats = math.comb(6, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose a subcommittee with