{2(\\sqrt[3]{2} - 1) + \\sqrt[3]{4}}{2} = \\sqrt[3]{2} - 1 + \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4}}{2}\n\\]\nThe integer part of $\\sqrt[3]{2} - 1 + \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4}}{2}$ is 1, so we can write:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[3]{2} - 1 + \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4}}{2} = 1 + \\left(\\sqrt[3]{2} - 2 + \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4}}{2}\\right)\n\\]\nThe fractional part $\\sqrt[3]{2} - 2 + \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4}}{2}$ can be inverted to find the next term in the continued fraction. The reciprocal of $\\sqrt[3]{2} - 2 + \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4}}{2}$ is:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{2} - 2 + \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4}}{2}}\n\\]\nThis can be simplified further to:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{2} - 2 + \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4}}{2}} = \\frac{2}{2\\sqrt[3]{2} - 4 + \\sqrt[3]{4}} = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{8} - 4 + \\sqrt[3]{4}} = \\frac{2}{2 - 4 + \\sqrt[3]{4}} = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2}\n\\]\nThe integer part of $\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2}$ is 6, so we can write:\n\\[\n\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2} = 6 + \\left(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2} - 6\\right)\n\\]\nThe fractional part $\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2} - 6$ can be inverted to find the next term in the continued fraction. The reciprocal of $\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2} - 6$ is:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2} - 6}\n\\]\nThis can be simplified further to:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2} - 6} = \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2}{2 - 6(\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2)} = \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2}{2 - 6\\sqrt[3]{4} + 12} = \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2}{14 - 6\\sqrt[3]{4}}\n\\]\nThe integer part of $\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2}{14 - 6\\sqrt[3]{4}}$ is 0, so we can write:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2}{14 - 6\\sqrt[3]{4}} = 0 + \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2}{14 - 6\\sqrt[3]{4}}\\right)\n\\]\nThe fractional part $\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2}{14 - 6\\sqrt[3]{4}}$ can be inverted to find the next term in the continued fraction. The reciprocal of $\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2}{14 - 6\\sqrt[3]{4}}$ is:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2}{14 - 6\\sqrt[3]{4}}} = \\frac{14 - 6\\sqrt[3]{4}}{\\sqrt[3]{4} - 2}\n\\]\nThis can be simpli