 // 6\n    base_six_digits.reverse()\n    return \'\'.join(base_six_digits)\n\n# Convert 999 from base 10 to base 6\nbase_six_number = decimal_to_base_six(999)\nprint(base_six_number)\n```\n```output\n4323\n```\nThe base six equivalent of \\(999_{10}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4323_6}\\).', 'To convert a decimal number to a base-six number, we repeatedly divide the number by 6 and keep track of the remainders. The base-six representation is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top. Let\'s perform this conversion step-by-step for the decimal number $999_{10}$.\n\n1. Divide 999 by 6, which gives a quotient of 166 and a remainder of 3.\n2. Divide 166 by 6, which gives a quotient of 27 and a remainder of 4.\n3. Divide 27 by 6, which gives a quotient of 4 and a remainder of 3.\n4. Divide 4 by 6, which gives a quotient of 0 and a remainder of 4.\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get the base-six representation of $999_{10}$ as $4343_6$.\n\nLet\'s verify this with Python code.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base_six(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % 6))\n        n //= 6\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 999 from decimal to base six\nbase_six_number = decimal_to_base_six(999)\nprint(base_six_number)\n```\n```output\n4343\n```\nThe base six equivalent of $999_{10}$ is $\\boxed{4343_6}$.', 'To convert the decimal number \\(999_{10}\\) to its base six equivalent, we need to repeatedly divide the number by 6 and keep track of the remainders. The remainders, read in reverse order, will give us the base six representation.\n\nLet\'s perform this conversion step by step using Python code.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base_six(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    \n    base_six_digits = []\n    while n > 0:\n        remainder = n % 6\n        base_six_digits.append(str(remainder))\n        n = n // 6\n    \n    # The remainders give the base six number in reverse orde