utput\n4323\n```\nThe base six equivalent of $999_{10}$ is $\\boxed{4323_6}$.', 'To convert a decimal number (base 10) to a base 6 number, we repeatedly divide the number by 6 and keep track of the remainders. The base 6 number is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top. Here\'s the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Divide 999 by 6, which gives 166 with a remainder of 3.\n2. Divide 166 by 6, which gives 27 with a remainder of 4.\n3. Divide 27 by 6, which gives 4 with a remainder of 3.\n4. Divide 4 by 6, which gives 0 with a remainder of 4.\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get the base 6 number $4343_6$.\n\nLet\'s verify this with Python code.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base_6(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % 6))\n        n //= 6\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 999 from base 10 to base 6\nbase_6_number = decimal_to_base_6(999)\nprint(base_6_number)\n```\n```output\n4343\n```\nThe base six equivalent of \\(999_{10}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4343_6}\\).', 'To convert the decimal number \\(999_{10}\\) to its base six equivalent, we can repeatedly divide the number by 6 and keep track of the remainders. The remainders, read in reverse order, will give us the base six representation.\n\nHere is the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Divide 999 by 6 to get the quotient and remainder.\n2. Continue dividing the quotient by 6 until the quotient is 0.\n3. The base six representation is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top.\n\nLet\'s do this step-by-step using Python code.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base6(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    base6_digits = []\n    while n > 0:\n        remainder = n % 6\n        base6_digits.append(str(remainder))\n        n = n // 6\n    base6_digits.reverse()\n    return \'\'.join(base6_digits)\n\n# Convert 999 from decimal to base six\ndecimal_number = 999\nbase6_representation = decimal_to_base6(decimal_number)\np