mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos \\theta = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 - \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta = \\frac{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 - \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ}{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\|}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this by noting that:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\|^2 = (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 + \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|^2 - 2 \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| = \\sqrt{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 + \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|^2 - 2 \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting this into the equation for $\\cos \\theta$:\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta = \\frac{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 - \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ}{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\sqrt{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 + \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|^2 - 2 \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ}}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this further by noting that the magnitudes of $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are arbitrary and can be normalized. Let's assume $\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| = 1$ and $\\|\\mathbf{b}\\| = 1$ for simplicity. Then we have:\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta = \\frac{1 - \\cos 29^\\circ}{\\sqrt{1 + 1 - 2 \\cos 29^\\circ}} = \\frac{1 - \\cos 29^\\circ}{\\sqrt{2(1 - \\cos 29^\\circ)}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{1 - \\cos 29^\\circ}}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 \\sin^2 14.5^\\circ}}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\sin 14.5^\\circ\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the angle $\\theta$ is:\n\\[\n\\theta = \\sin^{-1}(\\sin 14.5^\\circ) = 14.5^\\circ\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this using Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given angles\nangle_ab = 29  # angle between a and b in degrees\nangle_ba_minus_b = 84  # angle between b and a - b in degrees\n\n# Calculate the angle between a and a - b\nangle_a_a_minus_b = 180 - (angle_ab + angle_ba_minus_b)\n\nprint(angle_a_a_minus_b)\n```\n```output\n67\n```\nThe angle between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$ is 