equation, we can solve for \\(b\\).\n\n5. **Calculating the Perimeter:**\n   - The length \\(AB = AC = \\sqrt{b^2 + 11^2}\\).\n   - The perimeter of triangle \\(ABC\\) is \\(AB + AC + BC = 2\\sqrt{b^2 + 11^2} + 2b\\).\n\nLet's implement this in Python to find the value of \\(b\\) and then the perimeter of triangle \\(ABC\\).\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\nb = sp.symbols('b')\n\n# Define the equation using the tangent triple angle formula\ntan_theta = b / 11\ntan_3theta = b / 1\nequation = sp.Eq(tan_3theta, (3 * tan_theta - tan_theta**3) / (1 - 3 * tan_theta**2))\n\n# Solve the equation for b\nb_value = sp.solve(equation, b)[0]\n\n# Calculate the length of AB and AC\nAB = sp.sqrt(b_value**2 + 11**2)\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of triangle ABC\nperimeter = 2 * AB + 2 * b_value\n\n# Simplify the perimeter expression\nperimeter_simplified = sp.simplify(perimeter)\n\nprint(perimeter_simplified)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nIt seems there was an issue with the solution. Let's re-evaluate the equation and solve it step-by-step more carefully.\n\nThe equation we derived is:\n\\[\n\\frac{b}{1} = \\frac{3\\left(\\frac{b}{11}\\right) - \\left(\\frac{b}{11}\\right)^3}{1 - 3\\left(\\frac{b}{11}\\right)^2}\n\\]\nSimplifying the right-hand side, we get:\n\\[\nb = \\frac{3\\left(\\frac{b}{11}\\right) - \\left(\\frac{b}{11}\\right)^3}{1 - 3\\left(\\frac{b}{11}\\right)^2} = \\frac{\\frac{3b}{11} - \\frac{b^3}{1331}}{1 - \\frac{3b^2}{121}} = \\frac{\\frac{3b \\cdot 121 - b^3}{1331}}{\\frac{121 - 3b^2}{121}} = \\frac{363b - b^3}{121 - 3b^2}\n\\]\nMultiplying both sides by \\(121 - 3b^2\\), we get:\n\\[\nb(121 - 3b^2) = 363b - b^3\n\\]\nExpanding and simplifying, we get:\n\\[\n121b - 3b^3 = 363b - b^3 \\implies -3b^3 + b^3 = 363b - 121b \\implies -2b^3 = 242b \\implies -2b^2 = 242 \\implies b^2 = 121 \\implies b = 11 \\text{ (since } b > 0)\n\\]\n\nNow, we can calculate the length of \\(AB\\) and \\(AC\\):\n\\[\nAB = AC = \\sqrt{b^2 + 11^2} = \\sqrt{11^2 + 11^2}