 vector of the line passing through the points \\((-5, 4)\\) and \\((-1, 3)\\) is given by the difference between the coordinates of these points:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{pmatrix} -1 - (-5) \\\\ 3 - 4 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Normalize the direction vector:**\n\n   The direction vector \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) needs to be proportional to \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -7 \\\\ b \\end{pmatrix}\\). This means there exists a scalar \\( k \\) such that:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = k \\begin{pmatrix} -7 \\\\ b \\end{pmatrix}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the scalar \\( k \\):**\n\n   By comparing the components, we get:\n   \\[\n   4 = -7k \\quad \\text{and} \\quad -1 = kb\n   \\]\n\n   From the first equation, we can solve for \\( k \\):\n   \\[\n   k = -\\frac{4}{7}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Find \\( b \\):**\n\n   Substitute \\( k \\) into the second equation to solve for \\( b \\):\n   \\[\n   -1 = -\\frac{4}{7} b \\implies b = \\frac{7}{4}\n   \\]\n\nLet's verify this calculation using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\n\n# Define the variables\nb = symbols('b')\n\n# Define the equations based on the proportional relationship\nk = -4 / 7\nequation = Eq(-1, k * b)\n\n# Solve for b\nsolution = solve(equation, b)\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\n[1.75000000000000]\n```\nThe value of \\( b \\) is \\(\\frac{7}{4}\\), which is equivalent to \\(1.75\\).\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{7}{4}}\n\\]", "To find the value of \\( b \\) in the direction vector \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -7 \\\\ b \\end{pmatrix}\\), we need to determine the slope of the line parameterized by the given points \\((-5, 4)\\) and \\((-1, 3)\\).\n\nThe slope \\( m \\) of the line passing through two points \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\) is given by:\n\\[ m = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} \\]\n\nSubstituting the given points \\((-5, 4)\\) and \\((-1, 3)\\), we get:\n\\[ m 