e area of the square, and the small triangles (pieces "d" and "e") are each one-eighth the area of the square. The square piece "e" is one of the smaller pieces.\n\n4. **Calculate the Area of the Gray Piece:**\n   The gray piece is one of the small triangles, so its area is one-eighth of the area of the square. Therefore, the area of the gray piece is \\( \\frac{16}{8} = 2 \\) square inches.\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given area of the square\narea_square = 16\n\n# The area of the gray piece (one of the small triangles) is one-eighth of the area of the square\narea_gray_piece = area_square / 8\nprint(area_gray_piece)\n```\n```output\n2.0\n```\nThe area of the gray piece is \\(\\boxed{2}\\) square inches.', 'To solve this problem, we need to determine the area of the gray piece in the given tangram puzzle. Here are the steps to solve it:\n\n1. **Understand the Tangram Configuration**: The tangram consists of seven pieces: five isosceles triangles (two large, one medium, and two small), one square (piece "e"), and one parallelogram. The total area of the square \\(ABCD\\) is 16 square inches.\n\n2. **Determine the Areas of the Tangram Pieces**: Since the tangram pieces fit together to form the square \\(ABCD\\), the sum of the areas of all the pieces must equal the area of the square. Each piece\'s area can be calculated by understanding the relative sizes of the pieces.\n\n3. **Calculate the Area of the Gray Piece**: The gray piece is one of the isosceles triangles. Since the tangram is composed of pieces that fit together perfectly to form the square, and since the area of the square is 16 square inches, we can use the properties of the tangram to determine the area of each piece.\n\nThe area of the gray piece (one of the isosceles triangles) can be calculated as follows:\n\n- The square \\(ABCD\\) has an area of 16 square inches.\n- The tangram pieces fit together perfectly, so the area of each piece can be determined 