o \\( 9 + N \\) must be divisible by 3. Since 9 is already divisible by 3, \\( N \\) must also be divisible by 3. So \\( N \\) must be one of \\( \\{0, 3, 6, 9\\} \\).\n\n### Step 3: Combining the Conditions\nCombining the two conditions, \\( N \\) must be a nonzero digit that is both even and divisible by 3. The only nonzero digit that satisfies both conditions is \\( 6 \\).\n\nThus, the nonzero value of \\( N \\) that makes \\( 21420N \\) divisible by 6 is \\( 6 \\).\n\nLet's verify this using Python code.\n```python\n# Function to check if a number is divisible by 6\ndef is_divisible_by_6(n):\n    return n % 6 == 0\n\n# Iterate over possible values of N (1 to 9)\nfor N in range(1, 10):\n    number = 214200 + N\n    if is_divisible_by_6(number):\n        result = N\n        break\n\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n6\n```\nThe nonzero value of \\( N \\) that makes the number \\( 21420N \\) divisible by 6 is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).", "To determine the nonzero value of \\( N \\) that makes the number \\( 21420N \\) divisible by 6, we need to check two conditions:\n\n1. The number must be divisible by 2.\n2. The number must be divisible by 3.\n\nSince \\( 21420N \\) ends in \\( N \\), it is divisible by 2 if \\( N \\) is an even number (i.e., \\( N \\) can be 0, 2, 4, 6, or 8). However, since we are looking for a nonzero value of \\( N \\), \\( N \\) can only be 2, 4, 6, or 8.\n\nNext, for the number \\( 21420N \\) to be divisible by 3, the sum of its digits must be divisible by 3. The sum of the digits of \\( 21420N \\) is \\( 2 + 1 + 4 + 2 + 0 + N = 9 + N \\). So, \\( 9 + N \\) must be divisible by 3. Since 9 is already divisible by 3, \\( N \\) must also be divisible by 3. The only even numbers that are divisible by 3 are 6.\n\nTherefore, the nonzero value of \\( N \\) that satisfies both conditions is \\( 6 \\).\n\nLet's verify this using Python code.\n```python\n# Function to check if a number is divisible by 6\ndef is_divisible_by_6(number):\n    return number % 6 == 0