e coefficients and adding the exponents of \\(r\\).\n2. Then, divide the result by \\(8r^4\\) by dividing the coefficients and subtracting the exponents of \\(r\\).\n\nLet\'s break this down step by step and verify it using Python.\n\n1. Simplify the numerator:\n\\[\n(10r^3)(4r^6) = (10 \\cdot 4)(r^{3+6}) = 40r^9\n\\]\n\n2. Now divide by \\(8r^4\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{40r^9}{8r^4} = \\frac{40}{8} \\cdot r^{9-4} = 5r^5\n\\]\n\nSo the simplified expression is \\(5r^5\\). Let\'s verify this using Python.\n```python\n# Define the expression components\nnumerator_coefficient = 10 * 4\nnumerator_exponent = 3 + 6\ndenominator_coefficient = 8\ndenominator_exponent = 4\n\n# Simplify the expression\nsimplified_coefficient = numerator_coefficient // denominator_coefficient\nsimplified_exponent = numerator_exponent - denominator_exponent\n\n# Final simplified expression\nsimplified_expression = f"{simplified_coefficient}r^{simplified_exponent}"\nprint(simplified_expression)\n```\n```output\n5r^5\n```\nThe simplified expression is \\(\\boxed{5r^5}\\).', 'To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{(10r^3)(4r^6)}{8r^4}\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Combine the constants and the powers of \\(r\\) in the numerator.\n2. Simplify the fraction by dividing the constants and subtracting the exponents of \\(r\\).\n\nLet\'s break it down step-by-step and use Python to ensure accuracy.\n\nFirst, we combine the constants and the powers of \\(r\\) in the numerator:\n\n\\[\n(10r^3)(4r^6) = 10 \\cdot 4 \\cdot r^{3+6} = 40r^9\n\\]\n\nNow we have the expression:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{40r^9}{8r^4}\n\\]\n\nNext, we simplify the fraction by dividing the constants and subtracting the exponents of \\(r\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{40}{8} = 5 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad r^{9-4} = r^5\n\\]\n\nSo the simplified expression is:\n\n\\[\n5r^5\n\\]\n\nLet\'s confirm this using Python.\n```python\n# Define the expression components\nnumerator_constant = 10 * 4\nnumerator_exponent = 3 + 6\ndenominator_constant = 8\ndenominator_exponen