 \\frac{0.58}{2} = 0.29\n     \\]\n   - Convert the cost of the pencil from dollars to cents:\n     \\[\n     p = 0.29 \\text{ dollars} = 29 \\text{ cents}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Final Answer:**\n   - The cost of a pencil is \\( \\boxed{29} \\) cents.\n\nLet\'s implement this in Python to verify our solution:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variables\np, e = sp.symbols(\'p e\')\n\n# Define the equations\neq1 = sp.Eq(3*p + e, 1.24)\neq2 = sp.Eq(5*p + e, 1.82)\n\n# Solve the system of equations\nsolution = sp.solve((eq1, eq2), (p, e))\npencil_cost_dollars = solution[p]\npencil_cost_cents = pencil_cost_dollars * 100\n\nprint(pencil_cost_cents)\n```', 'The lengths of the sides of a triangle are $13$, $14$, and $15$ centimeters. What is the distance between the incenter and the circumcenter of the triangle? (Express your answer in simplest radical form.) \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\bo