firm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the remainder of 54 divided by 6\nremainder = 54 % 6\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder of \\(54 \\mod 6\\) is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", "To determine the remainder of \\(54 \\mod 6\\), we can use the modulus operation. The modulus operation finds the remainder after division of one number by another. In this case, we need to find the remainder when 54 is divided by 6. Let's calculate it step by step.\n\n1. Divide 54 by 6.\n2. The quotient is 9 and the remainder is 0.\n3. Therefore, \\(54 \\mod 6 = 0\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the remainder of 54 divided by 6\nremainder = 54 % 6\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder of \\(54 \\mod 6\\) is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", "To determine the remainder of 54 when divided by 6, we can use the modulus operation. The modulus operation (%) gives the remainder of a division of two numbers. In this case, we need to calculate 54 % 6. Let's write the Python code to find the answer.\n```python\n# Calculate the remainder of 54 divided by 6\nremainder = 54 % 6\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder when 54 is divided by 6 is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", "To determine the remainder of \\(54 \\mod 6\\), we can use the modulus operator in Python. The modulus operator (%) returns the remainder of the division of the first operand by the second operand.\n\nLet's calculate it step by step.\n\n1. Divide 54 by 6.\n2. The remainder of this division is the result of \\(54 \\mod 6\\).\n\nHere is the Python code to perform this calculation:\n```python\n# Calculate the remainder of 54 divided by 6\nremainder = 54 % 6\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder of \\(54 \\mod 6\\) is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", "To find the remainder when 54 is divided by 6, we can use the modulo operation. The modulo operation, denoted by the % symbol in most programming languages, gives the remainder of the division of one number by