rry, June, and Connie.\n2. Convert the total amount into cents.\n3. Determine how much money is left after converting as many of the coins into dollars as possible.\n\nLet's break it down and write the Python code to solve this problem.\n\n1. Calculate the total amount of money in dollars.\n2. Convert the total amount into cents.\n3. Determine the remainder when the total amount in cents is divided by 100 (since there are 100 cents in a dollar).\n\nHere is the Python code to perform these steps:\n\n```python\n# Amounts earned by each girl scout in dollars\nlinda_earned = 27.47\nsherry_earned = 35.23\njune_earned = 37.37\nconnie_earned = 26.52\n\n# Calculate the total amount earned\ntotal_dollars = linda_earned + sherry_earned + june_earned + connie_earned\n\n# Convert the total amount into cents\ntotal_cents = int(total_dollars * 100)\n\n# Determine the remainder when the total amount in cents is divided by 100\nremaining_cents = total_cents % 100\n\nprint(remaining_cents)\n```\n```output\n29\n```\nThe amount of money left after converting as many of the coins into bills as they could is \\(\\boxed{29}\\) cents.", "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total amount of money the girls earned.\n2. Convert the total amount into cents.\n3. Determine how much money is left after converting as many of the coins into bills as they could.\n\nLet's break it down step-by-step and write the Python code to get the accurate result.\n\n1. Calculate the total amount of money in dollars.\n2. Convert the total amount into cents (1 dollar = 100 cents).\n3. Determine the remaining cents after converting as many of the coins into bills as they could (i.e., the remaining cents will be the remainder when the total cents are divided by 100).\n\nHere is the Python code to perform these steps:\n```python\n# Amounts earned by each girl in dollars\nlinda_earned = 27.47\nsherry_earned = 35.23\njune_earned = 37.37\nconnie_earned = 26.52\n\n# Total amount earn