istance of a route\ndef calculate_distance(route):\n    total_distance = 0\n    for i in range(len(route) - 1):\n        total_distance += distances.get((route[i], route[i + 1]), distances.get((route[i + 1], route[i])))\n    return total_distance\n\n# Calculate the total distance for each route and find the minimum distance\nmin_distance = float('inf')\nfor route in routes:\n    total_distance = calculate_distance(route)\n    if total_distance < min_distance:\n        min_distance = total_distance\n\nprint(min_distance)\n```\n```output\n17\n```\nThe shortest distance that can be travelled if you start at any point $A$, $B$, $C$, or $D$ and visit the other three points once is \\(\\boxed{17}\\).", "To find the shortest distance that can be traveled starting from any point and visiting the other three points once, we need to calculate the total distance for each possible path and then find the minimum of these distances.\n\nThe four points are $A$, $B$, $C$, and $D$. The distances between the points are as follows:\n- $AB = 6$\n- $AC = 6$\n- $AD = 5$\n- $BC = 5$\n- $BD = 3$\n- $CD = 4$\n\nWe will calculate the total distance for each possible path starting from each point and visiting the other three points exactly once. The possible paths are:\n1. $A \\rightarrow B \\rightarrow C \\rightarrow D$\n2. $A \\rightarrow B \\rightarrow D \\rightarrow C$\n3. $A \\rightarrow C \\rightarrow B \\rightarrow D$\n4. $A \\rightarrow C \\rightarrow D \\rightarrow B$\n5. $A \\rightarrow D \\rightarrow B \\rightarrow C$\n6. $A \\rightarrow D \\rightarrow C \\rightarrow B$\n7. $B \\rightarrow A \\rightarrow C \\rightarrow D$\n8. $B \\rightarrow A \\rightarrow D \\rightarrow C$\n9. $B \\rightarrow C \\rightarrow A \\rightarrow D$\n10. $B \\rightarrow C \\rightarrow D \\rightarrow A$\n11. $B \\rightarrow D \\rightarrow A \\rightarrow C$\n12. $B \\rightarrow D \\rightarrow C \\rightarrow A$\n13. $C \\rightarrow A \\rightarrow B \\rightarrow D$\n14. $C \\rightarrow A \\rightarrow D \\righ