 price\nsale_price = 14.40\npercentage_of_original_price = 0.4\n\n# Calculate the original price\noriginal_price = sale_price / percentage_of_original_price\nprint(original_price)\n```\n```output\n36.0\n```\nThe original price of the shirt was $\\boxed{36.00}$.", "To determine the original price of the shirt, we can use the information that the sale price is $60\\%$ off the original price. This means that the sale price is $40\\%$ of the original price. We can set up the following equation:\n\n\\[ \\text{Sale Price} = 0.4 \\times \\text{Original Price} \\]\n\nGiven that the sale price is $14.40$, we can substitute this value into the equation and solve for the original price:\n\n\\[ 14.40 = 0.4 \\times \\text{Original Price} \\]\n\nTo find the original price, we can divide both sides of the equation by $0.4$:\n\n\\[ \\text{Original Price} = \\frac{14.40}{0.4} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given sale price and discount percentage\nsale_price = 14.40\ndiscount_percentage = 0.4\n\n# Calculate the original price\noriginal_price = sale_price / discount_percentage\nprint(original_price)\n```\n```output\n36.0\n```\nThe original price of the shirt was \\(\\boxed{36}\\) dollars.", "To find the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function within this interval. The key points to consider are the points where the absolute value expressions change, which are \\( x = p \\), \\( x = 15 \\), and \\( x = p + 15 \\). However, since \\( x \\) is restricted to the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we only need to consider the points \\( x = p \\) and \\( x = 15 \\).\n\nLet's break down the function into different cases based on the value of \\( x \\):\n\n1. When \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\):\n   - \\( |x - p| = x - p \\)\n   - \\( |x - 15| = 15 - x \\)\n   - \\( |x - p - 15| = 15 + p - x \\)\n\nSo, the function simplifies to:\n\\[ f(x) = (x - p) + (15 - x) + (15 + p - x) = 30 - x \\]\n\nSince \\( x \\) is in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) will occur at the maximum value of \\( x \\) in this interval, which is \\( x = 15 \\).\n\nLet's calculate \\( f(15) \\):\n\\[ f(15) = 30 - 15 = 15 \\]\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\( \\boxed{15} \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with a Python code implementation.\n```python\n# Define the function f(x)\ndef f(x, p):\n    return abs(x - p) + abs(x - 15) + abs(x - p - 15)\n\n# Define the interval p <= x <= 15\np = 7  # Example value for p, any value in the range 0 < p < 15 will work\nx_values = [p, 15]  # We only need to check the endpoints of the interval\n\n# Calculate the function values at the endpoints\nf_values = [f(x, p) for x in x_values]\n\n# Find the minimum value\nmin_value = min(f_values)\nprint(min_value)\n```", "To find the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function within the given interval.\n\n1. **Break Down the Absolute Values:**\n   - For \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\):\n     - \\( |x - p| = x - p \\)\n     - \\( |x - 15| = 15 - x \\)\n     - \\( |x - p - 15| = 15 + p - x \\) (since \\( x \\leq 15 \\) and \\( p < 15 \\), so \\( x - p - 15 \\) is negative)\n\n   Therefore, \\( f(x) = (x - p) + (15 - x) + (15 + p - x) = 30 - x \\).\n\n2. **Find the Minimum Value:**\n   - Since \\( f(x) = 30 - x \\) is a decreasing function, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) on the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) will occur at \\( x = 15 \\).\n   - So, \\( f(15) = 30 - 15 = 15 \\).\n\nThus, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\( 15 \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the function f(x)\ndef f(x, p):\n    return abs(x - p) + abs(x - 15) + abs(x - p - 15)\n\n# Define the interval p <= x <= 15\np = 7  # Example value for p, any value between 0 and 15 will give the same minimum value\nx_values = range(p, 16)  # Generate all integer values of x in the interval [p, 15]\n\n# Calculate the values of f(x) for all x in the interval\nf_values = [f(x, p) for x in x_values]\n\n# Find the minimum value of f(x) in the interval\nmin_value = min(f_values)\nprint(min_value)\n```\n```output\n15\n```\nThe minimum value taken by \\( f(x) \\) for \\( x \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to analyze the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) over the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\).\n\nLet's break down the function \\( f(x) \\) into different cases based on the value of \\( x \\) relative to \\( p \\) and \\( 15 \\):\n\n1. When \\( x \\geq p \\) and \\( x \\leq 15 \\):\n   - \\( |x - p| = x - p \\)\n   - \\( |x - 15| = 15 - x \\)\n   - \\( |x - p - 15| = 15 + p - x \\)\n   - So, \\( f(x) = (x - p) + (15 - x) + (15 + p - x) = 30 - x \\)\n\n2. When \\( x \\geq p \\) and \\( x \\geq 15 \\):\n   - \\( |x - p| = x - p \\)\n   - \\( |x - 15| = x - 15 \\)\n   - \\( |x - p - 15| = x - p - 15 \\)\n   - So, \\( f(x) = (x - p) + (x - 15) + (x - p - 15) = 3x - 2p - 30 \\)\n\n3. When \\( x \\leq p \\) and \\( x \\leq 15 \\):\n   - \\( |x - p| = p - x \\)\n   - \\( |x - 15| = 15 - x \\)\n   - \\( |x - p - 15| = 15 + p - x \\)\n   - So, \\( f(x) = (p - x) + (15 - x) + (15 + p - x) = 30 + 2p - 3x \\)\n\nSince we are only interested in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we can ignore the case \\( x \\geq 15 \\) because it is not within the interval. So we only need to consider the first and third cases within the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\).\n\nLet's evaluate \\( f(x) \\) at the boundaries \\( x = p \\) and \\( x = 15 \\):\n\n- When \\( x = p \\):\n  \\[\n  f(p) = |p - p| + |p - 15| + |p - p - 15| = 0 + (15 - p) + 15 = 30 - p\n  \\]\n\n- When \\( x = 15 \\):\n  \\[\n  f(15) = |15 - p| + |15 - 15| + |15 - p - 15| = (15 - p) + 0 + | - p | = 15 - p + p = 15\n  \\]\n\nSince \\( 0 < p < 15 \\), it is clear that \\( 30 - p > 15 \\). Therefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\( 15 \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python and sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable and parameter\nx, p = sp.symbols('x p')\n\n# Define the function f(x)\nf = sp.Abs(x - p) + sp.Abs(x - 15) + sp.Abs(x - p - 15)\n\n# Evaluate f(x) at the boundaries x = p and x = 15\nf_p = f.subs(x, p)\nf_15 = f.subs(x, 15)\n\n# Simplify the expressions\nf_p_simplified = sp.simplify(f_p)\nf_15_simplified = sp.simplify(f_15)\n\n# Print the simplified expressions\nprint(f_p_simplified)\nprint(f_15_simplified)\n```\n```output\nAbs(p - 15) + 15\n15\n```\nThe output confirms our earlier analysis. When \\( x = p \\), the function simplifies to \\( \\text{Abs}(p - 15) + 15 \\), which is \\( 15 - p + 15 = 30 - p \\). When \\( x = 15 \\), the function simplifies to \\( 15 \\).\n\nSince \\( 0 < p < 15 \\), it is clear that \\( 30 - p > 15 \\). Therefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is indeed \\( 15 \\).\n\nThus, the minimum value taken by \\( f(x) \\) for \\( x \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).", "To determine the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function within this interval.\n\n1. **Understand the function:**\n   - The function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) involves three absolute value terms.\n   - The critical points where the absolute value expressions change are \\( x = p \\), \\( x = 15 \\), and \\( x = p + 15 \\). However, since we are only considering the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we need to evaluate the function within this range.\n\n2. **Evaluate the function at the boundaries and critical points within the interval:**\n   - At \\( x = p \\), \\( f(p) = |p - p| + |p - 15| + |p - p - 15| = 0 + (15 - p) + 15 = 30 - p \\).\n   - At \\( x = 15 \\), \\( f(15) = |15 - p| + |15 - 15| + |15 - p - 15| = (15 - p) + 0 + | - p| = 15 - p + p = 15 \\).\n\n3. **Analyze the function within the interval:**\n   - For \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), the function \\( f(x) \\) can be simplified as follows:\n     - \\( f(x) = (x - p) + (15 - x) + (15 - p - x) = x - p + 15 - x + 15 - p - x = 30 - p - x \\).\n     - Since \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) within this interval will occur at \\( x = 15 \\), because as \\( x \\) increases, \\( f(x) \\) decreases.\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\( f(15) = 15 \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the function f(x)\ndef f(x, p):\n    return abs(x - p) + abs(x - 15) + abs(x - p - 15)\n\n# Define the interval and the range of p\np_values = [i for i in range(1, 15)]  # p can be any value from 1 to 14\nmin_values = []\n\n# Calculate the minimum value of f(x) for each p in the interval p <= x <= 15\nfor p in p_values:\n    min_value = min(f(x, p) for x in range(p, 16))\n    min_values.append(min_value)\n\n# The minimum value of f(x) for all p in the interval p <= x <= 15\nprint(min(min_values))\n```\n```output\n15\n```\nThe minimum value taken by \\( f(x) \\) for \\( x \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).", "To determine the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function within this interval. The function involves absolute values, which change their behavior at the points \\( x = p \\), \\( x = 15 \\), and \\( x = p + 15 \\). However, since we are only considering the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we can simplify our analysis.\n\nLet's break down the function \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\):\n\n1. For \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\):\n   - \\( |x - p| = x - p \\) because \\( x \\geq p \\).\n   - \\( |x - 15| = 15 - x \\) because \\( x \\leq 15 \\).\n   - \\( |x - p - 15| = 15 + p - x \\) because \\( x \\leq 15 \\) and \\( p < 15 \\), so \\( x \\leq 15 < p + 15 \\).\n\nSo, the function \\( f(x) \\) simplifies to:\n\\[ f(x) = (x - p) + (15 - x) + (15 + p - x) = 30 - x. \\]\n\nSince \\( f(x) = 30 - x \\) is a decreasing function in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in this interval will occur at \\( x = 15 \\).\n\nLet's calculate \\( f(15) \\):\n\\[ f(15) = 30 - 15 = 15. \\]\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\( 15 \\).\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure the result is accurate.\n```python\n# Define the function f(x)\ndef f(x, p):\n    return abs(x - p) + abs(x - 15) + abs(x - p - 15)\n\n# Set the interval p <= x <= 15 and find the minimum value of f(x)\np = 5  # Example value for p, any value in the range 0 < p < 15\nmin_value = float('inf')\nfor x in range(p, 16):  # Iterate over the interval p to 15\n    value = f(x, p)\n    if value < min_value:\n        min_value = value\n\nprint(min_value)\n```\n```output\n15\n```\nThe minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).", "To find the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function within the given interval.\n\nThe function \\( f(x) \\) is composed of three absolute value functions. The critical points where the behavior of the function might change are \\( x = p \\), \\( x = 15 \\), and \\( x = p + 15 \\). However, since we are only considering the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we only need to consider the points \\( x = p \\) and \\( x = 15 \\).\n\nLet's evaluate the function at these points:\n\n1. When \\( x = p \\):\n\\[ f(p) = |p - p| + |p - 15| + |p - p - 15| = 0 + |p - 15| + |-15| = 15 - p + 15 = 30 - p. \\]\n\n2. When \\( x = 15 \\):\n\\[ f(15) = |15 - p| + |15 - 15| + |15 - p - 15| = |15 - p| + 0 + |-p| = 15 - p + p = 15. \\]\n\nSince \\( 0 < p < 15 \\), it is clear that \\( 30 - p > 15 \\). Therefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is 15, which occurs at \\( x = 15 \\).\n\nThus, the minimum value taken by \\( f(x) \\) for \\( x \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure the result is accurate.\n```python\n# Define the function f(x)\ndef f(x, p):\n    return abs(x - p) + abs(x - 15) + abs(x - p - 15)\n\n# Define the interval p <= x <= 15\np = 7  # example value for p within the range 0 < p < 15\nx_values = [p, 15]  # critical points within the interval\n\n# Evaluate the function at the critical points\nf_values = [f(x, p) for x in x_values]\n\n# Find the minimum value\nmin_value = min(f_values)\nprint(min_value)\n```", "To find the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function within the given interval.\n\n1. **Understanding the function:**\n   - The function \\( f(x) \\) is composed of three absolute value terms. The critical points where the behavior of the function changes are at \\( x = p \\), \\( x = 15 \\), and \\( x = p + 15 \\).\n   - Since \\( p \\) and \\( p + 15 \\) are outside the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we only need to consider the behavior of the function within this interval.\n\n2. **Behavior of the function within the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\):**\n   - For \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), the term \\( |x - p| \\) simplifies to \\( x - p \\) because \\( x \\geq p \\).\n   - The term \\( |x - 15| \\) simplifies to \\( 15 - x \\) because \\( x \\leq 15 \\).\n   - The term \\( |x - p - 